 "notes": "Annual record: IS, BS and CF from the FY2013 10-K Exhibit 13 (which agree with the Q4-13 release twelve-month column); segment and non-GAAP tables from the Q4-13 release twelve-month column (10-K Note 18 agrees). IS: eps_basic 6.35 and eps_dil 6.25 are the 10-K total lines; the release prints continuing 6.21 / discontinued 0.04. net_income 6,109 = 10-K \"Net income\"; nci 388 (discontinued NCI \"\u2014\"). BS: 10-K detail; other_ca 3,035 = Future income tax benefits, current 1,964 + Other assets, current 1,071; other_nca 7,441 = Future income tax benefits 1,236 + Other assets 6,205; common_stock 14,638 = Common Stock 14,764 less Unearned ESOP shares (126) (as the release nets them); customer_financing 1,156 shown separately. CF: 10-K lines; cf.ni is income from continuing operations 6,074; customer_financing -135 = increase (245) + decrease 110; other_fin 51 = Common Stock issued under employee stock plans 378 + Other financing activities, net (327); acq = Investments in businesses (151), divest = Dispositions of businesses 1,560. ngaap: FY items = sum of the quarterly items (CCS 38 + 17 = 55; PW 193 - 25 = 168; interest 36 + 12 = 48; tax 95 + 22 + 24 + 13 = 154); items impact on diluted EPS from continuing operations \"\u2014\" (NI impact (2)); no adjusted EPS published. kpi.backlog_total_bn 82.1 is a computed sum of the five segment backlogs from the 10-K Item 1 (includes fully-funded government and intercompany backlog). py2 (FY2015 10-K): 2013 recast ex-Sikorsky - sales 56,600, OP 8,549, income from continuing operations 5,655; Sikorsky results in discontinued operations (sales 6,564). The FY2015 10-K segment note shows 2013 Eliminations and other (44) vs +22 as reported (Sikorsky intersegment eliminations and other). Presentation: 2013 discontinued operations = Rocketdyne, UTC Power, Clipper and legacy Hamilton Sundstrand Industrial businesses (2012 UTC Power revision noted in the Q1-13 release)."
